{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888572,"nonce":"0ABlZwIYdImC39rcj/KhuWQAF40=","title":"No Investigation can run against a Case, so there is no run, no transcript and no Finding to build anything on","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0053 §3: an Investigation is one run of one Investigator against one subject, a Step is one immutable transcript entry, a Finding is published as an Enrichment (`investigator.\u003cname\u003e`). None exists.\n\n**The demonstration.** `internal/enrichment/enrichers/` has `alerthistory`, `promrule`, `relatedalerts`, `runbook`, `silencematch` and no investigator.\n\n**Why it matters.** Backend tracer for 0053, runnable without any provider decision: a model **port** with a deterministic fake, and only oto's own history as Tools.\n\n**Where.** Investigator config (versioned: model, prompt, Tool allowlist, budgets); Investigation and Step tables (Steps append-only); a model port plus a scripted fake; River job; built-in Tools over prior Findings, the Case timeline and the RuleSnapshot; an API to request an Investigation on a Case and read it back. Includes the per-run half of §6: enabled (org and Investigator), step budget, token budget, wall-time budget, ending `exhausted` with a partial Finding kept.\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** Against the fake model, an API request on a Case runs async and never touches the notification path; Steps are append-only; the Finding is stored as an Enrichment; a run that hits any per-run budget ends `exhausted`, keeps its partial Finding and records why; the kill switch stops new runs; tokens spent are recorded; changing model, prompt or allowlist makes a new Investigator version and the Finding names it; all of this is tested with the fake.\n\n**Blocked by.** None — can start immediately.\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}